.TH COMMANDTOMFCJ5720DW 1 "November 2026" "MFC-J5720DW driver" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
commandtomfcj5720dw \- execute Brother MFC-J5720DW CUPS maintenance jobs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B commandtomfcj5720dw
.I job-id user title copies options
.RI [ file ]
.br
.B commandtomfcj5720dw
.BR \-h " | " \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
This CUPS filter reads maintenance commands from a file or standard input.
It writes printer commands to standard output for delivery by the queue's
backend. Ink queries use the backend's side channel on file descriptor 4.
The filter does not open a printer connection itself.
.PP
The entire input is validated before any command or query is issued.
Commands execute in file order and stop on the first query or output error.
Maintenance operations execute once per command, regardless of the CUPS copies
argument or print options. Repeated ReportLevels commands issue only one query.
.SH COMMAND FILE
The first line must be #CUPS-COMMAND.
Command names and ink selections are case insensitive. Blank lines, leading
and trailing whitespace, and comments starting with # are accepted.
Files must contain ASCII text, with LF or CRLF line endings.
The last line need not end in a newline.
Limits are 65536 bytes per file, 255 bytes per line excluding LF, and
256 commands. Unknown commands, invalid arguments and embedded NULs are rejected.
.TP
.B ReportLevels
Read and report ink estimates without printing. Requires a network backend
supporting CUPS side-channel SNMP queries; see mfcj5720dw_ink(1).
.TP
.B Clean all
Request normal cleaning of the black and color print heads.
.TP
.B Clean black
Request normal cleaning of the black print head.
.TP
.B Clean color
Request normal cleaning of the color print heads together.
.TP
.B CleanStrong all|black|color
Request strong cleaning (POWERPURGE) of the selected print heads.
.TP
.B CleanStrongest all|black|color
Request the strongest cleaning (SUPERPOWERPURGE) of the selected print heads.
These stronger modes consume more ink than normal cleaning.
.TP
.B PrintSelfTestPage
Print the printer's internal print-quality sheet to check the nozzles.
This is distinct from the CUPS document test page.
.PP
The two additional cleaning commands are extensions defined by this
driver, not standard CUPS or Brother command names. They select the same
three cleaning strengths and ink groups as Brother's maintenance utility.
Standard Clean always means normal cleaning.
Alignment commands are not advertised or accepted.
.SH EXAMPLES
Submit a nozzle check to an existing queue, replacing PRINTER with its name:
.PP
.nf
printf '#CUPS-COMMAND\enPrintSelfTestPage\en' | \e
  lp -d PRINTER -t 'Nozzle check' \e
     -o document-format=application/vnd.cups-command
.fi
.PP
Request normal cleaning of all heads:
.PP
.nf
printf '#CUPS-COMMAND\enClean all\en' | \e
  lp -d PRINTER -t 'Clean print heads' \e
     -o document-format=application/vnd.cups-command
.fi
.PP
For strong cleaning of the black head, submit this separate job:
.PP
.nf
printf '#CUPS-COMMAND\enCleanStrong black\en' | \e
  lp -d PRINTER -t 'Strong black-head cleaning' \e
     -o document-format=application/vnd.cups-command
.fi
.PP
Use CleanStrongest for the strongest mode.
Both extensions require exactly one ink selection: all, black or color.
.PP
GNOME's head-cleaning action submits Clean all when the queue advertises Clean.
It does not provide strength or ink-selection controls; use command jobs for
those choices.
Existing queues need their PPD updated to advertise the new commands; installing
a new model PPD alone does not replace a queue's private copy.
.SH ALIGNMENT
Use the printer touchscreen: Settings, Maintenance, Improve Print Quality,
Alignment. Select the paper size and follow the printed-pattern instructions.
No remote alignment protocol was established from the inspected Windows and
macOS drivers. PrintAlignmentPage and SetAlignment are unsupported.
The driver's vertical-line rendering preferences do not perform this calibration.
.SH STATUS
Successful filter completion means the command bytes were written to the backend,
not that the printer has finished cleaning or printing its check sheet.
There is no maintenance-completion polling. Submit an ink-level refresh after
the printer finishes if needed; a ReportLevels in the same job may read levels
before maintenance completes.
.PP
Each nozzle check reports a PAGE record on standard error.
Cleaning does not report a printed page.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero means success, an empty command job, or help. One means an invalid input,
input/output failure or failed ink query. Two indicates an invalid invocation.
.SH FILES
.I /usr/lib/cups/filter/commandtomfcj5720dw
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mfcj5720dw_ink (1),
.BR rastertomfcj5720dw (1),
.BR lp (1),
.BR lpadmin (8)
